//! check: run(exit=1, stdout="error: overflow")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: std.x.json, err.row, err.propagate
//!
//! `int_of`'s magnitude row, ridden out of `main` so the RECORD names
//! it: a twenty-digit integer in someone's document is an OUTCOME this
//! module reports (`overflow`, §10's mark) and never a process it ends —
//! the same digits handed to `std.fmt.parse_int` would TRAP, correctly,
//! because there they are a caller's argument and here they came out of
//! a document. This is the first file in the module to put that tag on
//! a record; the else-shaped misses live in dom_typed_reads.lu.
//!
//! Two lanes at this sprint's pin; lupin flips on a pin, not an edit
//! (see dom_navigation.lu).

use std.x.json

fn main() -> !int {
    let n = json.node("[99999999999999999999]", "0")?
    json.int_of(n)?
    0
}
